      {
        "id": "p23-q5-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$y=2-x$ and $y=x^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x,y)=(1,1)$ or $(-2,4)$",
          "worked": "Substituting for $y$:\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2&=2-x\\\\x^2+x-2&=0\\\\(x+2)(x-1)&=0\\\\x&=-2\\text{ or }1\\end{align*}$$\nFrom $y=x^2$, when $x=-2$, $y=4$; when $x=1$, $y=1$. Hence $(x,y)=(-2,4)$ or $(1,1)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-q5-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$y=2x-3$ and $y=x^2-4x+5$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x,y)=(2,1)$ or $(4,5)$",
          "worked": "Substituting for $y$:\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2-4x+5&=2x-3\\\\x^2-6x+8&=0\\\\(x-2)(x-4)&=0\\\\x&=2\\text{ or }4\\end{align*}$$\nFrom $y=2x-3$, when $x=2$, $y=1$; when $x=4$, $y=5$. Hence $(x,y)=(2,1)$ or $(4,5)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-q5-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$y=3x^2$ and $y=4x-x^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x,y)=(0,0)$ or $(1,3)$",
          "worked": "Substituting for $y$:\n$$\\begin{align*}3x^2&=4x-x^2\\\\4x^2-4x&=0\\\\4x(x-1)&=0\\\\x&=0\\text{ or }1\\end{align*}$$\nFrom $y=3x^2$, when $x=0$, $y=0$; when $x=1$, $y=3$. Hence $(x,y)=(0,0)$ or $(1,3)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-q5-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$x-y=5$ and $y=x^2-11$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x,y)=(-2,-7)$ or $(3,-2)$",
          "worked": "The first equation gives $y=x-5$. Substituting:\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2-11&=x-5\\\\x^2-x-6&=0\\\\(x-3)(x+2)&=0\\\\x&=3\\text{ or }-2\\end{align*}$$\nFrom $y=x-5$, when $x=3$, $y=-2$; when $x=-2$, $y=-7$. Hence $(x,y)=(3,-2)$ or $(-2,-7)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 50
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-q5-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$x-y=2$ and $xy=15$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x,y)=(-3,-5)$ or $(5,3)$",
          "worked": "The first equation gives $y=x-2$. Substituting:\n$$\\begin{align*}x(x-2)&=15\\\\x^2-2x-15&=0\\\\(x-5)(x+3)&=0\\\\x&=5\\text{ or }-3\\end{align*}$$\nFrom $y=x-2$, when $x=5$, $y=3$; when $x=-3$, $y=-5$. Hence $(x,y)=(5,3)$ or $(-3,-5)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 50
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-q5-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$3x+y=9$ and $xy=6$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x,y)=(1,6)$ or $(2,3)$",
          "worked": "The first equation gives $y=9-3x$. Substituting:\n$$\\begin{align*}x(9-3x)&=6\\\\3x^2-9x+6&=0\\\\x^2-3x+2&=0\\\\(x-1)(x-2)&=0\\\\x&=1\\text{ or }2\\end{align*}$$\nFrom $y=9-3x$, when $x=1$, $y=6$; when $x=2$, $y=3$. Hence $(x,y)=(1,6)$ or $(2,3)$.",
